@startuml seq-complete
!include style.iuml

title Complete a task (including the Apple recurring-task quirk)

autonumber "<b>00"
participant "Apple Reminders" as C
participant "PutHandler" as PH
participant "DonetickApiClient" as API
participant "Donetick" as DT
participant "ChoreCache" as CC

note over C
  Ticking off a task may produce two PUTs: one for the original
  resource, and for recurring tasks an extra COMPLETED copy
  under a new client-generated UID.
end note

== PUT on the original resource ==
C -> PH : PUT .../donetick-42.ics  STATUS:COMPLETED
PH -> PH : ResolveChoreId -> 42 (path match)
PH -> PH : StatusMapper.FromVTodoStatus("COMPLETED")\n-> shouldComplete = true
PH -> API : CompleteChoreAsync(42)
API -> DT : POST /eapi/v1/chore/42/complete
DT --> API : 2xx
note right of DT
  Donetick records the completion and,
  for recurring chores, advances
  NextDueDate and resets the status.
end note
PH -> API : GetAllChoresAsync()
API -> DT : GET /eapi/v1/chore
DT --> API : all chores
PH -> CC : UpdateChores(all)  (CTag changes)
PH --> C : 204 No Content (no ETag header)
note right of C
  Without an ETag the client cannot treat its local
  COMPLETED copy as current, so it refetches and
  picks up the new DUE and NEEDS-ACTION.
end note

== Extra COMPLETED copy (recurring tasks) ==
C -> PH : PUT .../{new-uuid}.ics  STATUS:COMPLETED  UID:{new-uuid}
PH -> PH : ResolveChoreId -> null (unknown UID)
PH -> PH : shouldComplete = true
PH --> C : 204 No Content (ignored, nothing created)

== Next client refresh ==
C -> C : sees new CTag / missing ETag
C -> C : refetch donetick-42.ics via PROPFIND / REPORT (read path)
note right of C : Task reappears with the next due date
@enduml
